  "implementation_notes": [
    "Penalty selection: grouped cross-validated partial-likelihood deviance as in the current glmnet source (buildPredmat.coxnetlist, cv.coxnet, cvstats, getOptcv.glmnet). Per fold: deviance of the fold model on all patients of the current fit minus its deviance on the fold training patients, divided by the fold size; fold-size-weighted mean and SE. Deviance = 2 x (saturated - model) Breslow log partial likelihood. lambda_min = largest penalty at the minimum; lambda_1se = largest penalty with mean deviance <= minimum + its SE.",
    "Penalty grid of each current fit: scikit-survival automatic grid on the pre-processed data of that fit (100 values, alpha_min_ratio 0.01); its CV folds use the same grid.",
    "scikit-survival ends a path when the deviance ratio changes by < 0.1% over 5 penalties. With tied survival times its null deviance ignores ties, so the ratio starts slightly below 0 and the rule can fire wrongly; such stops (ratio < 0) are continued at the next penalty. Genuine stops (ratio > 0) keep the last fitted coefficients for the remaining penalties, as glmnet does for fold paths shorter than the lambda sequence. Counts are reported for every fit.",
    "Numerical failures: penalties at and after the first failure in any fold or in the full-data fit are dropped for all folds (plan section 5).",
    "CV fold assignment: primary population sorted by sample_id; StratifiedKFold(shuffle=True) on the OS event with the plan seeds; repeat 1 = r = 0 (outer seed SEED + 100).",
    "Nested CV: each outer training fold repeats the whole procedure (variance filter, z-score, grid, inner 10-fold CV); outer test patients are z-scored with the outer training statistics.",
    "CV-KM: out-of-fold LP of repeat 1; each fold split at the median in-sample LP of its outer training fold; high = LP > cutoff; no log-rank p-value.",
    "Added value (descriptive): out-of-fold LP of repeat 1 standardized with the LP mean and SD of its outer training fold; Cox models fitted with lifelines (Efron ties); COO coded GCB (reference), ABC, other (UNC, MHG).",
    "Stability: bootstrap rows drawn with replacement (seed 20261315, all 100 index vectors drawn at once); in each resample the variance filter and z-score are re-estimated and the path is fitted on the final grid down to lambda_min.",
    "Sensitivity (e): the full-data path of the primary model with the fold assignment of each alternative seed.",
    "Solver settings: scikit-survival defaults (tol 1e-7, max_iter 100000)."
  ],
